{
  "inShort": "The photo and film thumbnail leave progress on the playable slice unknown. Behind: the checkpoint goal was missed because no playable build or five-player notes were shown. Mia has not confirmed work since week one, leaving engineering support for the slice unconfirmed.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmvu474vj00k1k9z85tgw7gsa",
      "text": "The public repository evidence matches the task: Godot demos, an MIT license and import instructions. It supplies a foundation, not proof of the playable slice."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvu474w200k2k9z8zz6mezdu",
      "text": "The animated reference video remains done. The sprint links Big Buck Bunny again, but only its title and thumbnail were checked. Neither verifies the animation reference or shows this game."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvu474wh00k3k9z823f1jo7o",
      "text": "The reference article explains playtesting and matches the task. It does not establish that five players tested the slice."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvu474wy00k4k9z8bbq9qdph",
      "text": "The private design board remains done. Its contents were not checked, so it cannot establish progress on the playable slice."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [],
  "outsidePlan": [
    "The mountain landscape photo does not show the tide loop, two islands or co-op sailing. No new artifact supports the reported build or polish."
  ],
  "questions": [
    "Which downloadable build supports the release claim, and where are its launch instructions and controls?",
    "What do the five players’ notes establish about sailing together and understanding the tide loop?",
    "Carry the playable build and five players’ notes into the next checkpoint. I look forward to your next checkpoint’s devlogs, artifacts and activity ;)"
  ]
}

